3.2 Convolutional Neural Network
To estimate the Q-values a CNN is used. For the action space Sa the network consists of two blocks to extract features from the images, a concatenation of the features and another CNN to reach the Q-values. The feature extraction blocks are pre-trained Pytorch models where the final classification network is removed. The layer to be removed is different for each model and, in general, the fully connected layers are removed. Four models were selected to compose the network, DenseNet, MobileNet, ResNext and MNASNet. The criteria considered the feature space and the performance of the models. The use of pre-trained PyTorch models reduces the overall training time. However it brings limitations to the system, the size of the input image must be 224 by 224 pixels and the image must be normalized following the original


